description:
The starter contains a stand-in file API whose reference pages say:

- `Handle fakeOpen(const std::string& name)`: opens a file; returns `INVALID` if it does not exist.
- `long fakeRead(Handle h, char* buffer, std::size_t size)`: reads **up to** `size` bytes (it may return fewer even before the end); returns the number read, **0 at the end of the file**, or **-1 on an error**.
- `void fakeClose(Handle h)`: closes the handle. Every handle that was opened must be closed exactly once.

The documentation's example (lesson 5.01) is:

```cpp-norun
Handle h = fakeOpen(name);
char buffer[256];
long n = fakeRead(h, buffer, sizeof buffer);
return std::string(buffer, n);
```

Write the robust version, and one function built on it:

```cpp-norun
std::optional<std::string> readWholeFile(const std::string& name);
std::optional<std::size_t> countLines(const std::string& name);
```

- **readWholeFile** returns the whole contents, however many reads it takes and however long the file is; an empty optional if the file cannot be opened or any read fails. The handle is always closed.
- **countLines** returns the number of lines: the number of `\n` characters, plus one if the file is not empty and does not end with `\n`. An empty file has 0 lines. An empty optional if reading fails.

starter.solution.cpp:
#include <algorithm>
#include <map>
#include <optional>
#include <string>
#include <utility>

// The stand-in file API. Do not change it.
using Handle = int;
constexpr Handle INVALID = -1;
inline std::map<std::string, std::string> g_files;
inline std::map<Handle, std::pair<std::string, std::size_t>> g_open;
inline Handle g_nextHandle{ 3 };
inline int g_failOnRead{ 0 };
inline int g_reads{ 0 };
inline std::size_t g_chunk{ 5 };

Handle fakeOpen(const std::string& name)
{
    if (!g_files.count(name)) return INVALID;
    const Handle h{ g_nextHandle++ };
    g_open[h] = { name, 0 };
    g_reads = 0;
    return h;
}

long fakeRead(Handle h, char* buffer, std::size_t size)
{
    const auto it{ g_open.find(h) };
    if (it == g_open.end()) return -1;
    if (++g_reads == g_failOnRead) return -1;
    const std::string& data{ g_files[it->second.first] };
    const std::size_t pos{ it->second.second };
    const std::size_t n{ std::min({ size, g_chunk, data.size() - pos }) };
    std::copy_n(data.data() + pos, n, buffer);
    it->second.second += n;
    return static_cast<long>(n);
}

void fakeClose(Handle h) { g_open.erase(h); }

// Your code.
std::optional<std::string> readWholeFile(const std::string& name) { return std::nullopt; }
std::optional<std::size_t> countLines(const std::string& name) { return std::nullopt; }

